L.API_CONSENT_TEXT = "It asks to read what Bankai Guild shows you: the Wanted list and its bounties, the public rankings, your own frame and title, your guild, rank and role, and the King's presence as the King's lines and the Realm tab show it: whether he is online, the zone they name, his crown's map position while he shares it, whether you are on his layer and, while you are in his zone, its layers' names and '~N with Bankai Guild' counts. If your signed Bankai Guild role permits, it may also start and stop a short exact-name last-seen search, maintain a bounded set of those searches while a visible tool session that you started remains on, or run one five-minute hostile-area search at a time. An area search may be widened to players the game shows as not hostile whose guild, as each observer's client reads it, is not an Bankai Guild guild or who have none; never the observer's group or an Bankai Guild guild, and each row says whether the player is hostile. A visible Start must declare the names you chose or configured and any list source it includes. An area search may use your current selected map or a fresh exact-result map from one of those names; it must cancel before rotating and wait at least 60 seconds after the previous area start. Its UI must remain visible and stoppable, show the selected map and rotation position, never open the world map automatically, and stop on Off, permission loss or UI reload. Each exact-name search sends the exact Name-Realm sought to the Bankai Guild network; an area search broadcasts one selected map ID. Members who separately enabled Guild tools: player sightings may answer privately from a current direct target, nameplate or mouseover observation, or from a recent observation kept only in memory while that permission and location sharing remained on. Each client keeps at most 64 observations for up to 15 minutes, never saves them, and clears them when that permission, location sharing or network participation is turned off. One area search accepts at most six observations from each member and keeps at most 48 distinct hostile players. An exact-name result includes the observer and guild; an area result omits them. A result labels whether its coordinates are the target's native observed-unit or matching party/raid-unit point, or the observer's nearby encounter point, and includes its age and expiry. Bankai Guild sends each answer only to the requester. A trusted addon may show sanitized area rows with BankaiGuild-owned world-map pins, which are removed on cancel, expiry, permission revocation or UI reload, and keep recent rows in sight as BankaiGuild-owned world-map and minimap dots while its visible session is on. Your own area search also lists the players your own game shows you, without sending anything. A permitted addon may also request a short host-owned profile-presentation session. Only a current signed issuer or the addon's author can open it. While it is live, an admitted member may enable the single fixed BankaiGuild-owned style on their own character. The addon cannot choose a target, texture, atlas, colour, layout or arbitrary message; Bankai Guild accepts only a pre-approved caption, renews the session every 10 seconds and drops a missed lease after about 32 seconds. A permitted addon may also turn on a quiet presence for this session, only for the King, a High Councillor or the addon's author: while it is on, Bankai Guild stops sending on its own the words that announce you online or say where you are (no hello, census report, layer, map dot, layer-hop offer, sighting or sighting answer, nor the King's crown), and other Bankai Guild clients age you out as after a logout; your guild roster, the census your guildmates build from it (a guild leader or officer still shows online there, and your zone may for up to 12 minutes), /who and chat still show you; Bankai Guild chat lines you type and what you post yourself still go out, and a /reload or logout ends it. Searches and results expire; this is last-seen information, not continuous tracking, and no protected game action is performed. Never the census, other players' private data or Bankai Guild's keys. Yes, or Authorize all on this page: Bankai Guild permits these reads, searches and the bounded presentation on this computer; what that addon then does with the copies is up to that addon, so authorize only addons you trust. No, Keep current choices, or no answer: it receives nothing, starts no search and cannot enable the presentation or the quiet presence. Each addon remains listed and can be changed separately."
-- The line of an addon that is not authorized for the reserved features (API.lua's Reserved): only
-- what it may read, never the King's presence, a search, the quiet presence nor the profile presentation.
L.API_CONSENT_TEXT_BASIC = "It asks to read what Bankai Guild shows you: the Wanted list and its bounties, the public rankings, your own frame and title, your guild, rank and role. Never your location or the King's, the census, other players' private data or Bankai Guild's keys. No protected game action is performed. Yes, or Authorize all on this page: Bankai Guild permits these reads on this computer; what that addon then does with the copies is up to that addon, so authorize only addons you trust. No, Keep current choices, or no answer: it receives nothing. Each addon remains listed and can be changed separately."
